#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# unquote

#% text
# `unquote(e)` replaces every outermost `quote(x)` and `hold_complete(x)` in `e` (at any depth) by `x` and evaluates the result. A quote of several arguments inside a call gives them all to the call.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
unquote(quote(1 + 2))
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
unquote(f(quote(1 + 1), quote(a, b)))
#% output
#= f(2, a, b)

#% cell
unquote(quote(quote(1 + 1)))
#% output
#= quote(1 + 1)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `quote`, `hold_complete`, `eval`
